IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Schedule 1 -- the defined terms that can be worked out from facts, as functions.
-- Every defined term has an entry in qld-schedule1-table.l4; the functions here are for terms whose definition turns on a fact, a number, a date or a list.
-- The business day, calendar month, calendar year, financial year, month and midnight definitions are in qld-interpretation-time.l4.
-- A "means" definition answers JUST FALSE for a thing outside it; an "includes" definition answers NOTHING for a thing it does not name.

§ `Schedule 1 -- terms worked out from facts`

§§ `Persons, ages and groups`

-- src:1078 | adult means an individual who is 18 or more.
@ref Schedule 1, definition adult (src:1078-1078)
GIVEN `it is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an adult (Schedule 1, definition adult)` IS
    JUST (`it is an individual` AND `the age in years` AT LEAST 18)

-- src:1337 | minor means an individual who is under 18.
@ref Schedule 1, definition minor (src:1337-1337)
GIVEN `it is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a minor (Schedule 1, definition minor)` IS
    JUST (`it is an individual` AND `the age in years` LESS THAN 18)

-- child, "if age rather than descendancy is relevant": when descendancy is the question the definition does not speak.
-- src:1150 | child, if age rather than descendancy is relevant, means an individual who is under 18.
@ref Schedule 1, definition child (src:1150-1150)
GIVEN `age rather than descendancy is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a child (Schedule 1, definition child)` IS
    IF `age rather than descendancy is relevant` THEN JUST (`it is an individual` AND `the age in years` LESS THAN 18) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1286 | individual means a natural person.
@ref Schedule 1, definition individual (src:1286-1286)
GIVEN `it is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an individual (Schedule 1, definition individual)` IS
    JUST `it is a natural person`

DECLARE `Kind of entity in a definition` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a corporation`
    `a de facto partner`
    `a civil partner`
    `anything else`

-- src:1382 | person includes an individual and a corporation.
@ref Schedule 1, definition person (src:1382-1382)
GIVEN entity IS A `Kind of entity in a definition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `person includes the entity (Schedule 1, definition person)` IS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1377 | party includes an individual and a corporation.
@ref Schedule 1, definition party (src:1377-1377)
GIVEN entity IS A `Kind of entity in a definition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `party includes the entity (Schedule 1, definition party)` IS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1449 | spouse includes de facto partner and civil partner.
@ref Schedule 1, definition spouse (src:1449-1449)
GIVEN entity IS A `Kind of entity in a definition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `spouse includes the entity (Schedule 1, definition spouse)` IS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `a de facto partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a civil partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1158 | civil partner means a person who is a party to a civil partnership.
@ref Schedule 1, definition civil partner (src:1158-1158)
GIVEN `the person is a party to a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a civil partner (Schedule 1, definition civil partner)` IS
    JUST `the person is a party to a civil partnership`

-- src:1475 | Torres Strait Islander is a person who is a descendant of an Indigenous inhabitant of the Torres Strait Islands.
@ref Schedule 1, definition Torres Strait Islander (src:1475-1475)
GIVEN `the person is a descendant of an Indigenous inhabitant of the Torres Strait Islands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a Torres Strait Islander (Schedule 1, definition Torres Strait Islander)` IS
    JUST `the person is a descendant of an Indigenous inhabitant of the Torres Strait Islands`

-- src:1069 | Aboriginal people means people of the Aboriginal race of Australia.
@ref Schedule 1, definition Aboriginal people (src:1069-1069)
GIVEN `they are people of the Aboriginal race of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `they are Aboriginal people (Schedule 1, definition Aboriginal people)` IS
    JUST `they are people of the Aboriginal race of Australia`

-- src:1169 | community or group of Aboriginal people includes—
-- src:1170 | (a) the descendants of the community or group; and
-- src:1171 | (b) if there is only 1 surviving member of a community or group of Aboriginal people—that person.
@ref Schedule 1, definition community or group of Aboriginal people (src:1169-1171)
GIVEN `they are the descendants of the community or group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is only 1 surviving member of the community or group and the person is that member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the people are included in the community or group of Aboriginal people (Schedule 1, definition community or group of Aboriginal people)` IS
    IF `they are the descendants of the community or group` OR `there is only 1 surviving member of the community or group and the person is that member` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Places and bodies`

DECLARE `Kind of place` IS ONE OF
    `a State of the Commonwealth`
    `the Australian Capital Territory`
    `the Northern Territory`
    `the Jervis Bay Territory`
    `another Territory of the Commonwealth`
    `anything else`

-- State means a State of the Commonwealth, and includes the Australian Capital Territory and the Northern Territory.  "Means" closes it.
-- src:1452 | State means a State of the Commonwealth, and includes the Australian Capital Territory and the Northern Territory.
@ref Schedule 1, definition State (src:1452-1452)
GIVEN place IS A `Kind of place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is a State (Schedule 1, definition State)` IS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `a State of the Commonwealth` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Australian Capital Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Northern Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1302 | internal Territory means the Australian Capital Territory, the Jervis Bay Territory or the Northern Territory.
@ref Schedule 1, definition internal Territory (src:1302-1302)
GIVEN place IS A `Kind of place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is an internal Territory (Schedule 1, definition internal Territory)` IS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `the Australian Capital Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Jervis Bay Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Northern Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1239 | external Territory means a Territory, other than an internal Territory, for the government of which as a Territory provision is made by a Commonwealth Act.
@ref Schedule 1, definition external Territory (src:1239-1239)
GIVEN `it is a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an internal Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made for its government as a Territory by a Commonwealth Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is an external Territory (Schedule 1, definition external Territory)` IS
    JUST (`it is a Territory` AND (NOT `it is an internal Territory`) AND `provision is made for its government as a Territory by a Commonwealth Act`)

-- Australia and the Commonwealth: "but, when used in a geographical sense, does not include an external Territory".
-- src:1106 | Australia means the Commonwealth of Australia but, when used in a geographical sense, does not include an external Territory.
@ref Schedule 1, definition Australia (src:1106-1106)
GIVEN `it is within the Commonwealth of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word is used in a geographical sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an external Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is within Australia (Schedule 1, definition Australia)` IS
    JUST (`it is within the Commonwealth of Australia` AND (NOT (`the word is used in a geographical sense` AND `it is an external Territory`)))

-- src:1165 | Commonwealth means the Commonwealth of Australia but, when used in a geographical sense, does not include an external Territory.
@ref Schedule 1, definition Commonwealth (src:1165-1165)
GIVEN `it is within the Commonwealth of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word is used in a geographical sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an external Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is within the Commonwealth (Schedule 1, definition Commonwealth)` IS
    JUST (`it is within the Commonwealth of Australia` AND (NOT (`the word is used in a geographical sense` AND `it is an external Territory`)))

-- src:1422 | Queensland waters means all waters that are—
-- src:1423 | (a) within the limits of the State; or
-- src:1424 | (b) coastal waters of the State.
@ref Schedule 1, definition Queensland waters (src:1422-1424)
GIVEN `the waters are within the limits of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the waters are coastal waters of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the waters are Queensland waters (Schedule 1, definition Queensland waters)` IS
    JUST (`the waters are within the limits of the State` OR `the waters are coastal waters of the State`)

-- coastal waters of the State means (a) the parts of the territorial sea of Australia within the adjacent area, other than any part mentioned in the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4(2);
-- or (b) any sea on the landward side of any part of the territorial sea and within the adjacent area, but not within the limits of the State.
-- src:1160 | coastal waters of the State means—
-- src:1161 | (a) the parts of the territorial sea of Australia that are within the adjacent area in respect of the State, other than any part mentioned in the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4(2); or
-- src:1162 | (b) any sea that is on the landward side of any part of the territorial sea of Australia and within the adjacent area in respect of the State, but is not within the limits of the State.
@ref Schedule 1, definition coastal waters of the State (src:1160-1162)
GIVEN `it is a part of the territorial sea of Australia that is within the adjacent area in respect of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a part mentioned in the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a sea on the landward side of any part of the territorial sea of Australia and within the adjacent area in respect of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is within the limits of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the waters are coastal waters of the State (Schedule 1, definition coastal waters of the State)` IS
    JUST (   (`it is a part of the territorial sea of Australia that is within the adjacent area in respect of the State` AND (NOT `it is a part mentioned in the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4(2)`))
          OR (`it is a sea on the landward side of any part of the territorial sea of Australia and within the adjacent area in respect of the State` AND (NOT `it is within the limits of the State`)))

-- src:1325 | local government means—
-- src:1326 | (a) the Brisbane City Council; or
-- src:1327 | (b) a local government under the Local Government Act 2009.
@ref Schedule 1, definition local government (src:1325-1327)
GIVEN `it is the Brisbane City Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a local government under the Local Government Act 2009` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a local government (Schedule 1, definition local government)` IS
    JUST (`it is the Brisbane City Council` OR `it is a local government under the Local Government Act 2009`)

§§ `Documents, numbers, dates and other terms`

DECLARE `Kind of number` IS ONE OF
    `a number expressed in figures or words`
    `a letter`
    `a combination of a number so expressed and a letter`
    `anything else`

-- src:1356 | number means—
-- src:1357 | (a) a number expressed in figures or words; or
-- src:1358 | (b) a letter; or
-- src:1359 | (c) a combination of a number so expressed and a letter.
@ref Schedule 1, definition number (src:1356-1359)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of number`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a number (Schedule 1, definition number)` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `anything else` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1202 | date of assent, in relation to an Act, means the day on which the Act receives the royal assent.
@ref Schedule 1, definition date of assent (src:1202-1202)
GIVEN `the day on which the Act receives the royal assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the date of assent of an Act (Schedule 1, definition date of assent)` IS
    `the day on which the Act receives the royal assent`

-- src:1443 | sitting day, in relation to the Legislative Assembly, means a day on which the Legislative Assembly actually sits.
@ref Schedule 1, definition sitting day (src:1443-1443)
GIVEN `the Legislative Assembly actually sits on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is a sitting day (Schedule 1, definition sitting day)` IS
    JUST `the Legislative Assembly actually sits on the day`

-- src:1401 | public holiday means a day appointed under the Holidays Act 1983 or another Act as a public holiday.
@ref Schedule 1, definition public holiday (src:1401-1401)
GIVEN `the day is appointed under the Holidays Act 1983 or another Act as a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is a public holiday (Schedule 1, definition public holiday)` IS
    JUST `the day is appointed under the Holidays Act 1983 or another Act as a public holiday`

-- src:1490 | year, without specifying the type of year, means calendar year.
@ref Schedule 1, definition year (src:1490-1490)
GIVEN `the type of year is specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the year is a calendar year (Schedule 1, definition year)` IS
    IF `the type of year is specified` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1450 | Standards Association of Australia, for anything done or to be done on or after 1 July 1999, includes a reference to Standards Australia Limited ACN 087 326 690.
@ref Schedule 1, definition Standards Association of Australia (src:1450-1450)
GIVEN `the day the thing is done or to be done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to the Standards Association of Australia includes a reference to Standards Australia Limited ACN 087 326 690 (Schedule 1, definition Standards Association of Australia)` IS
    IF `the day the thing is done or to be done` AT LEAST Date 1 7 1999 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1446 | spent conviction means a conviction—
-- src:1447 | (a) for which the rehabilitation period under the Criminal Law (Rehabilitation of Offenders) Act 1986 has expired under that Act; and
-- src:1448 | (b) that is not revived as prescribed by section 11 of that Act.
@ref Schedule 1, definition spent conviction (src:1446-1448)
GIVEN `the rehabilitation period under the Criminal Law (Rehabilitation of Offenders) Act 1986 has expired under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction is revived as prescribed by section 11 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction is a spent conviction (Schedule 1, definition spent conviction)` IS
    JUST (`the rehabilitation period under the Criminal Law (Rehabilitation of Offenders) Act 1986 has expired under that Act` AND (NOT `the conviction is revived as prescribed by section 11 of that Act`))

DECLARE `Kind of record` IS ONE OF
    `a record of information, however recorded`
    `a thing on which there is writing`
    `a thing on which there are marks, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them`
    `an electronic document`
    `anything else`

-- document: (a) means a record of information, however recorded; and (b) includes the three further things.
-- src:1222 | document—
-- src:1223 | (a) means a record of information, however recorded; and
-- src:1224 | (b) includes—
-- src:1225 | (i) a thing on which there is writing; and
-- src:1226 | (ii) a thing on which there are marks, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them; and
-- src:1227 | (iii) an electronic document.
@ref Schedule 1, definition document (src:1222-1227)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of record`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a document (Schedule 1, definition document)` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Kind of thing for an electronic document` IS ONE OF
    `a thing from which sounds, images or writings can be reproduced with or without the aid of anything else`
    `a record of information reproduced from a thing of that kind`
    `a record of information that exists in digital form and is capable of being reproduced, transmitted, stored or duplicated by electronic means`
    `anything else`

-- src:1228 | electronic document means—
-- src:1229 | (a) a thing from which sounds, images or writings can be reproduced with or without the aid of anything else; or
-- src:1230 | (b) a record of information reproduced from a thing mentioned in paragraph (a); or
-- src:1231 | (c) a record of information that exists in digital form and is capable of being reproduced, transmitted, stored or duplicated by electronic means.
@ref Schedule 1, definition electronic document (src:1228-1231)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of thing for an electronic document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is an electronic document (Schedule 1, definition electronic document)` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `anything else` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1298 | instrument means any document.
@ref Schedule 1, definition instrument (src:1298-1298)
GIVEN `it is a document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is an instrument (Schedule 1, definition instrument)` IS
    JUST `it is a document`
